# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Work with bosonic circuits {#work-with-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr "Pagtatrabaho sa mga bosonic circuit {#work-with-bosonic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") expresses a computation directly on **bosonic modes**. It carries no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count: those enter later, during transpilation, which is how one circuit can be lowered under several encodings and several truncations without being rebuilt.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") ay nagpapahayag ng computation nang direkta sa **mga bosonic mode**. Wala itong truncation, encoding, o bilang ng qubit: pumapasok ang mga iyon sa ibang pagkakataon, sa transpilation, kaya naka-lower ang isang circuit sa ilang encoding at ilang truncation nang hindi binubuo muli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It deliberately exposes a reduced API compared to Qiskit’s [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), so that qubit gates cannot be applied to a bosonic mode, which would not be a well-defined operation. This guide covers the operations that *are* exposed for assembling larger circuits out of smaller ones.\n"
msgstr "Sadyang mas maliit ang API na inilalantad nito kumpara sa [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) ng Qiskit, para hindi makapag-apply ng mga qubit gate sa isang bosonic mode, na hindi magiging well-defined na operasyon. Sinasaklaw ng gabay na ito ang mga operasyong *inilalantad* para sa pagbuo ng mas malalaking circuit mula sa mas maliliit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use bosonic circuits {#why-use-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr "Bakit gagamit ng mga bosonic circuit {#why-use-bosonic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the traditional workflow for putting the time evolution of a bosonic Hamiltonian onto a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang ang tradisyonal na workflow para ilagay ang time evolution ng isang bosonic Hamiltonian sa qubit-based na architecture:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the bosonic Hamiltonian, for example $H = -\\sum_{ij} b^\\dagger_i b_j$.\n"
msgstr "Idefine ang bosonic Hamiltonian, halimbawa $H = -\\sum_{ij} b^\\dagger_i b_j$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a truncation and an encoding, and map the Hamiltonian to a qubit operator with them.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng truncation at encoding, at i-map ang Hamiltonian sa isang qubit operator gamit ang mga iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution in qubit space, by Trotterization or another method.\n"
msgstr "Ipatupad ang time evolution sa qubit space, sa pamamagitan ng Trotterization o ibang method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second step comes early, and it makes two decisions that are expensive to take back. The truncation fixes how many levels each mode keeps, and the encoding fixes how many qubits that costs, so both are fixed in the qubit operator before anything else has been done with the circuit. To look at the same physics under another cutoff or another encoding, you map the Hamiltonian again and build the circuit again. What the mapping discards, as well, is the bosonic structure: which terms belong together, and that the terms of a hopping pair are each other’s adjoint.\n"
msgstr "Maaga ang ikalawang hakbang, at gumagawa ito ng dalawang desisyong magastos bawiin. Itinatakda ng truncation kung ilang level ang pinapanatili ng bawat mode, at itinatakda ng encoding kung ilang qubit ang kailangan niyon, kaya parehong naka-fix sa qubit operator bago pa magawa ang anupaman sa circuit. Para makita ang parehong physics sa ibang cutoff o ibang encoding, ima-map mo ulit ang Hamiltonian at bubuuin ulit ang circuit. Ang itinatapon din ng mapping ay ang bosonic na estruktura: kung aling mga term ang magkakasama, at na ang mga term ng isang hopping pair ay adjoint ng isa't isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") moves those decisions to the end:\n"
msgstr "Inililipat ng isang [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") ang mga desisyong iyon sa dulo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the bosonic Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Idefine ang bosonic Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Express the time evolution directly on bosonic modes, with bosonic gates.\n"
msgstr "Ipahayag ang time evolution nang direkta sa mga bosonic mode, gamit ang mga bosonic gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the truncation and the encoding as part of the transpilation.\n"
msgstr "Piliin ang truncation at ang encoding bilang bahagi ng transpilation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit describes *what* computation to perform, and transpilation decides *how* to put it on qubits. The same circuit is then lowered at every cutoff and under every encoding, and the grouping of the operator is still there for the passes that can use it. The next sections show how such a circuit is assembled; [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) shows it being lowered.\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng circuit kung *anong* computation ang gagawin, at ang transpilation ang nagpapasya kung *paano* ito ilalagay sa mga qubit. Ang parehong circuit ay ilo-lower sa bawat cutoff at sa bawat encoding, at nariyan pa rin ang grouping ng operator para sa mga pass na makakagamit nito. Ipinapakita ng mga susunod na seksyon kung paano binubuo ang ganoong circuit; ipinapakita ng [I-transpile ang mga bosonic circuit](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) kung paano ito ilo-lower.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "Generic na mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") module and the circuit share one convention for modes. A mode is only an index that labels a bosonic degree of freedom, and it carries no meaning of its own. You can therefore evolve any operator that implements the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, whatever it represents, and the circuit never needs to know what mode `2` stands for. The same holds for the size of a mode: a circuit has no occupation cutoff, so nothing here says how many levels a mode has.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") module at ang circuit ay may iisang convention para sa mga mode. Ang mode ay index lang na nagla-label ng isang bosonic degree of freedom, at wala itong sariling kahulugan. Kaya maaari mong i-evolve ang anumang operator na nagpapatupad ng [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, anuman ang kinakatawan nito, at hindi kailangang malaman ng circuit kung ano ang kinakatawan ng mode `2`. Ganoon din sa laki ng mode: walang occupation cutoff ang circuit, kaya walang nagsasabi rito kung ilang level mayroon ang isang mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Append gates {#append-gates}"
msgstr "Magdagdag ng mga gate {#append-gates}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gates are appended onto modes. Only [`BosonicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-gate#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate\") instances are accepted:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga gate ay idinadagdag sa mga mode. Mga instance lang ng [`BosonicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-gate#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate\") ang tinatanggap:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything else is refused, and the error names the offending type:\n"
msgstr "Tinatanggihan ang anupamang iba, at pinapangalanan ng error ang may-sala na uri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compose circuits {#compose-circuits}"
msgstr "I-compose ang mga circuit {#compose-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose\") places the instructions of one circuit onto another. They are **inlined**, not wrapped into a single gate, so the result is an ordinary circuit that you can keep decomposing and transpiling.\n"
msgstr "Inilalagay ng [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose\") ang mga instruction ng isang circuit sa isa pa. **Ini-inline** ang mga ito, hindi binabalot sa isang gate, kaya ang resulta ay karaniwang circuit na maaari mong ipagpatuloy sa pag-decompose at pag-transpile.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default a new circuit is returned and both operands are left alone. Pass `inplace=True` to modify the first one instead, and `front=True` to put the operand *before* the existing instructions:\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, isang bagong circuit ang ibinabalik at hindi ginagalaw ang parehong operand. Ipasa ang `inplace=True` para baguhin na lang ang una, at `front=True` para ilagay ang operand *bago* ang mga kasalukuyang instruction:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A narrower circuit can be placed onto a chosen subset of the modes:\n"
msgstr "Ang mas makitid na circuit ay maaaring ilagay sa napiling subset ng mga mode:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A narrow-composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A narrow-composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-5.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only another [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") is accepted as the operand, because Qiskit’s own `compose` would inline qubit gates and bypass the check that `append` enforces.\n"
msgstr "Isa pang [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") lang ang tinatanggap bilang operand, dahil ang sariling `compose` ng Qiskit ay mag-i-inline ng mga qubit gate at lalampasan ang check na ipinapatupad ng `append`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Ulitin ang isang circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") repeats a circuit end to end. The repetitions are **flattened**: the result holds the instructions `reps` times in sequence rather than one gate wrapping the circuit. Therefore, the operation counts scale with `reps`, and `decompose` acts on the repeated body instead of removing one repetition.\n"
msgstr "Inuulit ng [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") ang isang circuit mula simula hanggang dulo. **Pinapatag** ang mga repetition: hawak ng resulta ang mga instruction nang `reps` beses nang sunod-sunod sa halip na isang gate na bumabalot sa circuit. Kaya, lumalaki ang bilang ng operasyon ayon sa `reps`, at ang `decompose` ay umaaksyon sa inuulit na katawan sa halip na magtanggal ng isang repetition.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A repeated BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-6.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A repeated BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-6.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the circuit-level way to Trotterize: evolve for a short time, and repeat. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) for the alternative of choosing a product formula on the gate itself, and why the two are different things that happen to share the word “repetitions”.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang paraan sa circuit level para mag-Trotterize: mag-evolve sa maikling oras, at ulitin. Tingnan ang [Mag-synthesize ng Evolution gate sa bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) para sa alternatibong pagpili ng product formula sa mismong gate, at kung bakit magkaiba ang dalawa kahit pareho ang salitang “repetitions”.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separate steps with barriers {#separate-steps-with-barriers}"
msgstr "Paghiwalayin ang mga hakbang gamit ang mga barrier {#separate-steps-with-barriers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **barrier** marks a synchronization point that optimization passes do not fuse gates across. [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier\") places one on all modes, or on the modes you name:\n"
msgstr "Ang **barrier** ay nagmamarka ng synchronization point na hindi tinatawid ng mga optimization pass sa pag-fuse ng mga gate. Naglalagay ang [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier\") ng isa sa lahat ng mode, o sa mga mode na pinangalanan mo:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-7.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-7.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`repeat(..., insert_barriers=True)` puts one between consecutive repetitions, and none after the last:\n"
msgstr "Naglalagay ang `repeat(..., insert_barriers=True)` ng isa sa pagitan ng magkakasunod na repetition, at wala pagkatapos ng huli:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A repeated BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A repeated BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers and the encoding {#barriers-and-the-encoding}"
msgstr "Mga barrier at ang encoding {#barriers-and-the-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An encoding needs several qubits per mode, so the register of modes and the register of qubits differ in size, and a layout relates *whole registers*. A mode therefore has no qubits of its own to narrow a barrier to. During the boson-to-qubit synthesis a barrier is mapped onto **every qubit of each register it touched**, which is correct under any layout:\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng encoding ng ilang qubit bawat mode, kaya magkaiba ang laki ng register ng mga mode at register ng mga qubit, at nag-uugnay ang layout ng *buong register*. Kaya walang sariling qubit ang mode para paliitin ang barrier. Sa boson-to-qubit synthesis, ang barrier ay ima-map sa **bawat qubit ng bawat register na hinawakan nito**, na tama sa anumang layout:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A QuantumCircuit showing the expansion of barrier to cover the entire qubit register.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A QuantumCircuit showing the expansion of barrier to cover the entire qubit register.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-9.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read out a bosonic circuit {#read-out-a-bosonic-circuit}"
msgstr "I-read out ang isang bosonic circuit {#read-out-a-bosonic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") has no `measure` or `measure_all`. What a measured bit means depends on the encoding. Under a unary encoding the occupation of a mode is spread over several qubits and has to be read from a pattern of bits, and under a compact one it is a binary number, so a measurement that names a mode would have to know the encoding, which a bosonic circuit deliberately does not. Measure the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) instead, and decode the bitstrings with [`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\") and the offsets of the [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") that you lowered with. [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) does this for a complete model.\n"
msgstr "Walang `measure` o `measure_all` ang isang [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\"). Nakadepende sa encoding ang kahulugan ng isang nasukat na bit. Sa unary encoding, ang occupation ng isang mode ay nakakalat sa ilang qubit at kailangang basahin mula sa pattern ng mga bit, at sa compact naman ay binary number ito, kaya ang measurement na nagpapangalan ng mode ay kailangang alam ang encoding, na sadyang hindi alam ng bosonic circuit. Sa halip, sukatin ang na-transpile na [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), at i-decode ang mga bitstring gamit ang [`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\") at ang mga offset ng [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") na ginamit mo sa pag-lower. Ginagawa ito ng [I-simulate ang Bose-Hubbard dynamics gamit ang pagpili ng encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) para sa kumpletong modelo.\n"

